 <section id="safety" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">5. OEM Safety Certifications: What Buyers Must Verify</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">Safety is non-negotiable for professional procurement. <a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:underline">Consumer Product Safety Commission</a> reports indicate substandard chargers cause thousands of electrical incidents annually. For a complete regulatory breakdown across markets, see our <a href="/blog/charger-safety-standards" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">charger safety standards guide</a>.</p>
 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-4">10-Layer Circuit Protection</h3>
 <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-6">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Over-Current</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Auto-shutdown when current exceeds safe levels, preventing device damage from alternator voltage surges in vehicle power systems.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Over-Voltage</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Prevents voltage spikes from damaging connected devices, essential for 24V truck systems where alternator output can spike to 28V+.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Over-Temperature</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Thermal shutdown at 85&deg;C+, critical for dashboard-mounted chargers exposed to direct sunlight in parked vehicles.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Short-Circuit</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Instant cutoff on output short, preventing fire hazards from frayed or pinched charging cables in vehicle cabins.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Reverse Polarity</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Prevents damage from incorrect installation or wiring faults, a common failure mode in fleet vehicle 12V socket retrofits.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Surge Protection</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">IEC 61000-4-5 compliant, absorbing voltage transients from engine starts and alternator load dumps that can exceed 100V.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">ESD Protection</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">&plusmn;8kV contact discharge rated, protecting charger electronics from static buildup common in dry vehicle interiors.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Battery Protection</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Prevents overcharging connected devices, maintaining battery health for phones and tablets used as fleet driver tools.</p></div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 text-center"><div class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase text-sm mb-2">Low-Voltage Cutoff</div><p class="text-slate-600 text-xs">Protects vehicle battery from drain when the engine is off, ensuring fleet vehicles always start after overnight charging sessions.</p></div>
 </div>
 <div class="mt-6 mb-6">
